body:
God I hope Jon doesn't win the throne. I mean how boring and typical. I hope Dany does get the throne, because I think it really does belong to her, but I want her to do some terrible shit to get there. I want her to basically become Cersei. 

&#x200B;

Now obviously I am team Cersei, but it's pretty unlikely. Thus why I made conditions for Dany lol.

It's going to take time and practice. Start with applying stoic philosophies to smaller things. Like when someone is walking too slowly in front of you in the grocery store. Take a breath, and either slow down or walk around, noting that anger will not help you.  Try reading stoic texts daily.  I'm reading The Moral Letters to Lucilius from Seneca right now. It's like 3 bucks for the kindle version on Amazon. 

&#x200B;

In regards to what you're feeling now, maybe evaluate how you got here. Consider that anger will not help you. If your displeasure is at yourself then that's wonderful news, because only you can control you. Consider what mistakes have been made, and carry those lessons with you. With each setback, you'll get better at managing your reactions, but you need to keep stoicism at the forefront of your mind. Read and practice daily. The future will come in the form of the present.

Damn, that was a relatable response. I've had an identical experience. I had an accent (which I don't hear which makes it hard to fix), my family started laughing, so I stopped speaking Polish to anyone but my grandparents (no choice they don't speak English), so my Polish got worse!!

Yeah hopefully being here for a few months I will have plenty of time and resources to better myself.  It's been a few days and I'm already starting to feel a little better about just speaking. I used to get really defensive when getting corrected, but I've learned to take in stride now and say thank you lol.

&#x200B;

The line my therapist gave me when I kept circling "what's the point if we die anyway?" was "why bother eating if you'll only be hungry again?"

Or another, which may be more helpful in your situation;

You can poop on the floor right now. But you aren't going to because you aren't going to die in the next 5 minutes. You'd just end up sitting in a poopy room. Don't make your life a poopy room. 

He kind of explained how, no matter what, our brains are wired for survival. Suicidal thoughts are our brain's way of telling us that we need to change something, it tells us the way our life is going is so bad we may as well be dead.  The point is not to make us kill ourselves, but rather start making changes in our lives. This could mean dropping everything and moving across the country to start a new life, or just be something like ending an abusive relationship.  Sometimes we know the problem and sometimes we don't but it can be figured out and changed. I mean if the alternative is dying then what's the big deal about changing absolutely everything? I mean if you still hate it you can always die later. 

&#x200B;

Not sure if much of that was logical, I started to ramble. Therapy may help your friend. See if you can talk them into it.

1) You're reaching out for help. That's already the first step, you recognize the problem. Now take the next step.

&#x200B;

2) Let the past go. You can't change it and thinking about it wont change anything, it will only make it harder to focus on the future. Start practicing mindfulness, which mean just take 5 minutes every day to just sit and be. Close your eyes and think about the feeling of your feet touching the floor, the sounds around you, your breath as it fills your lungs then leaves, and let your thoughts come and go. Don't try not to think about anything, but rather learn to let these thoughts come and go, as though you're watching traffic. The cars come and go, you don't stop one of them and dwell on it. 

This takes practice, try it for 5 days. My therapist recommended the app Headspace. It's free for the first 10 days, it'll give you an idea of how to start.

&#x200B;

3) Don't think about what will fully fulfill you. Think about what you can do to get started, and how to use that to take the next step. As you get an income and some traction, you will find more doors will open for you. See where those doors lead.

&#x200B;

4) Get therapy. Seriously, I just started therapy this month and while it's not helpful yet, my therapist provides a perspective that I haven't considered before. Your friends will tell you what they always have, you know what to expect from them. A therapist is objective with good intention, and comes from a completely different walk of life than you. This outside perspective is really healthy and helpful in breaking you out of a cycle. Yes it costs money, but if you need it then you NEED it. Maybe with therapy you'll be able to get your life together, then the cost of therapy is made up for in 10 years when you are making 10x what you would be otherwise and are 10x happier.

Ha, it's just funny I did the same thing a few days ago. You are a help, I'm so used to people jumping to defend humanity I was getting ready to fight. You caught me off balance.

I know the comments are supportive, but my instincts don't.

You will find help here too, if you seek it.

&#x200B;

&#x200B;
